A page author is researching a knowledge base and asks:

{{ query }}

Below are candidate chunks retrieved from the sources of one run, each under
its source stem. For each chunk, answer one typed question: does this chunk
contain material that answers the request — a fact, a number, a definition,
a method, or a quotation the page could use?

{% for stem, snippet in candidates %}
## {{ stem }}

{{ snippet }}

{% endfor %}
Return one verdict per candidate chunk. Copy each stem verbatim from the
headings above — the stem is the join key back to the chunk. A chunk that
merely mentions a term of the request without answering it is not relevant.
A chunk you cannot assess is not relevant; never skip a stem and never
invent one.
